// AVL tree :

// what is an AVL tree?
// AN avl tree is a self balancing binary search tree . 

// why we need of an AVL tree?
// because in binary search tree the height of tree in worst case was O(n) in avl tree we get log(n) in worst case because and it is to self balancing tree it balances through its own thats why we need an avl tree. 

// height of the balanced tree ==> for each node balance factor should be {1,0,-1} then it should be known as balanced binary tree and it is also known as balance factor :

// what is the balance factor ?
// balance factor is the rule of AVL tree which is defines the balance of the tree . 
// and there is formula for the balance factor which is :
// balance factor  = Hl - HR = {1,0,-1} height of the left subtree - height of the right subtree = 1,0,-1 it is the formula for the balance factor of an AVL tree. 

// there are imbalances also in AVL tree :
// 1) left -left imbalance 
// 2) right -right imbalance
// 3) left - right imbalance
// 4) right - left imbalance 

// 1) left - left imbalance :
// we have solution for this type of imbalance which is known as right rotation . 
// it occurs when the left subtree is imbalance in a AVL tree and we will do the right rotation to balance because the tree is calculated by the height not by the node . 

// 2) right - right imbalance :
// we have solution for this type of imbalance which is known as left rotation. 
// it occurs when the right subtree is imbalance in an AVL tree and we will do the left rotation to balance because the tree is calculated by the height of the tree not by the node. 

// 3) left - right imbalance :
// we have solution for this type of imbalance but the solution is not one method the solution is of two methods  right rotation and left rotation as well which balances the avl tree . 
// it occurs when the left subtee is imbalance in an AVL tree and we will do the right rotation and then left rotation to balance because the tree is calculated by the height of the tree not by the node. 
// when the left subtree is imbalance and in that right subtree is also imbalances we use this method to balance the AVL tree. 

// 4) right - left imbalance :
// it known as the mirror image of the left - right imbalance and we have solution for this type of imbalance but the solution is  not one method the solution is of two methods left rotation and right rotation as well which balances the AVL tree. 
// it occurs when the right subtree is imbalance in an AVL tree and we will do the left rotation and then right rotation to balance because the tree is calculated by the height of the tree not by the node. 
// when the right subtree is imbalance and in that left subtree is also imbalances we use this method to balance the AVL tree.

